{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Rule 6c-11:** An authorized participant must be a **member or participant of an SEC-registered clearing agency** and have a **written agreement with the ETF or one of its service providers** allowing it to place orders to purchase and redeem creation units. The rule itself does not specifically require both NSCC membership and DTC participation, or mandate that the distributor be the contractual counterparty.\n\n**Agreement forms:** U.S. AP agreements commonly involve the AP and the ETF’s distributor; the trust/fund may also be a party. Forms may impose more specific NSCC/DTC eligibility and settlement requirements than the rule.\n\nI cannot identify the counterparties in **the bank’s reviewed forms** from the information supplied. Those document-specific parties should not be confused with the rule’s broader permitted counterparties."}}
